crysknife, that suggests sticking with it for skill slot economy in the
late game.

>The whole thing behind the silver in the offhand is the bonus +d20,
>which is its primary appeal over the crysknife to begin with, really.

Well, quite. But is a little extra damage against most targets worth more
or less than a lot of extra damage against some targets? I wouldn't like
to call it.

>I'm not saying a crysknife isn't good -- just that pretending it's the
>only and/or best option for a Rogue is senseless, given the plethora of
>_other_ equally valid options available.

I agree, but I think it's an interesting leap away from the normal
secondary weapon orthodoxy.
